{"kind":"request","text":"Rule on legacy hosted-MCP OAuth mapping continuity before S4 adoption.\n\nThe attached source contract names the existing control, Agent and OAuth mapping schemas at 7177b87b. A legacy controller/client-to-Agent mapping records no originating operation or completion flag. Its target, timestamps and request fingerprint cannot prove which operation inserted it or completed its handoff.\n\nThe proposed nullable pending_op column distinguishes legacy unknown (NULL), an exact new provisional owner (a valid nonempty operation), and a mapping confirmed by a new successful handoff (empty string). Exact owner comparisons and byte accounting protect new mappings. The legacy branch needs your continuity ruling.\n\nOption A retains unknown legacy rows and returns existing 503 temporarily_unavailable for new consent using those bindings. Existing access/refresh admission remains separate; this does not itself revoke old tokens. This can block new consent on a previously established binding.\n\nOption B allows a NEW explicit signed authorization for the SAME stored controller, client and Agent, after exact public identity and fresh key/controller/subset/actor facts. One Registry transaction must compare the entire mapping and exclude every other unresolved reserved grant for that Agent across all clients. All grant paths must honor that fence. The legacy row stays NULL until an actual successful matching handoff and final authority/owner checks confirm this new authorization. Refusal never deletes the unknown row; uncertainty stays reserved. This proves no historical origin or completion.\n\nI recommend the bounded fresh-authorization path if its all-path fence is feasible. Please choose the policy or specify another bounded route. No recovery task, permanent deferral, migration, compiler/test/control body, opening of hosted MCP or deployment follows from this question. Source preparation for new mappings and the other S4 boundaries continues. The attached contract states the exact existing capacity and operation bounds, costs and remaining proof obligations.","body":{"conditions":"Choose the bounded legacy OAuth mapping continuity policy and ownership representation before S4 adoption. State whether fresh explicit same-binding reauthorization may confirm an unknown row under an atomic all-Agent unresolved-grant fence, or whether new consent must retain/refuse. No migration, recovery task, body or deployment authorization is requested.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}